    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d499">

                <pb facs="0461" n="345" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg345"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 738.3915/99.]</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to the
                            Dominican Republic to the Secretary of
                            State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Santo Domingo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-03-21">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 21, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I am informed by the Minister for Foreign Affairs that he has instructed the
                    Dominican Minister at Washington,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d499-f1"/> to consult
                    with the Department in regard to the advisability of an ultimatum from the
                    Dominican to the Haitian Government, which is openly violating treaties and
                    international obligations. The Dominican Government desires to know if we can
                    help them in any way.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Russell.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d499-f1" n="1" xml:id="d499-f1-content">
                <p>Dr. Francisco J. Peynado.</p>
